638
00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:42.660
No, for all of time.
没错，一直以来都是这样。

639
00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:43.620
For all of time.
一直以来。

640
00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:44.720
Who decided this?
这是谁定的？

641
00:27:44.840 --> 00:27:46.940
In movies and television, you do a 555.
在电影和电视里，都会用555。

642
00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:48.240
And then here's the thing.
而且重点是这个。

643
00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:50.420
I don't know if you've ever noticed this.
我不知道你有没有注意到这一点。

644
00:27:50.600 --> 00:27:59.440
In movies, sometimes instead of saying 555, because people have become wise, other people have become wise.
在电影里，有时他们不再用555，因为人们变聪明了，其他人也变聪明了。

645
00:27:59.440 --> 00:28:03.860
But everyone else knows for all of time, 555 is a baloney number.
但大家都知道，一直以来，555都是个假号码。

646
00:28:04.040 --> 00:28:04.540
That's right.
没错。

647
00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:09.480
So what they'll do if you see it written down in some movies, like I'm throwing this out there.
所以如果有些电影里写了号码，他们会怎么做呢，我只是随口一说。

648
00:28:09.520 --> 00:28:14.160
I don't know if it's true, but all the president's men, they'll get a hot tip, a phone number they have to call.
我不知道是不是真的，但在《总统班底》里，他们会得到一个重要线索，一个必须拨打的电话号码。

649
00:28:14.160 --> 00:28:22.040
And it'll say, like, JL5, and then the rest of the phone number, because J and L are fives.
上面会写着类似JL5，然后是剩下的电话号码，因为J和L代表5。

650
00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:26.500
You know how sometimes people replace, you know, where it's like 1-800-HELP.
你知道有时候人们会用字母代替数字，就像1-800-HELP那样。

651
00:28:26.680 --> 00:28:26.900
Yeah.
是啊。

652
00:28:27.120 --> 00:28:31.920
You know, like how businesses have numbers like 1-800-BLA-BLA-BLA-BLA-CALL-HELP or something.
你知道，就像有些公司会有那种电话号码，比如1-800-巴拉巴拉巴拉巴拉-求助之类的。

653
00:28:32.060 --> 00:28:32.380
I don't know.
我不知道。

654
00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:33.740
That's more numbers than you need.
那号码位数多得离谱。

655
00:28:33.820 --> 00:28:34.480
But you got it.
但你懂我意思。

656
00:28:34.780 --> 00:28:41.400
So, yeah, they'll be like, JL5, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, as a way to try to disguise it.
所以，没错，他们会用什么JL5，巴拉巴拉之类的，以此来掩盖真实号码。

657
00:28:41.400 --> 00:28:53.360
But, well, okay, my other thing about the real estate office is we have talked about the fact that Greg Daniels loved the episode that Jon Favreau turned in so much.
不过，好吧，关于房地产办公室，我们之前聊过，格雷格·丹尼尔斯非常喜欢乔恩·费儒交上来的那一集。

658
00:28:53.440 --> 00:28:54.540
He didn't want to cut anything.
他什么都不想删。

659
00:28:54.780 --> 00:28:56.600
And we had to even add stuff.
我们甚至还得往里加内容。

660
00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:57.000
That's right.
没错。

661
00:28:57.120 --> 00:28:57.260
Yeah.
是啊。

662
00:28:57.460 --> 00:29:05.300
There were two talking heads, one by Mark, played by Bob, and then one by Michael Weston, who played sort of the Jim-esque character.
当时有两个采访镜头，一个是鲍勃饰演的马克，另一个是迈克尔·韦斯顿，他演的是那种类似吉姆的角色。

663
00:29:06.580 --> 00:29:10.200
And they are on the deleted scenes, and I thought you might want to hear them.
那些片段在删减镜头里，我想你们可能会想听听。

664
00:29:10.320 --> 00:29:10.740
Let's listen.
我们来听听吧。

665
00:29:10.740 --> 00:29:12.260
Yeah, I'm in real estate.
没错，我是做房地产的。

666
00:29:12.580 --> 00:29:12.700
Yeah.
是啊。

667
00:29:13.420 --> 00:29:15.200
I mean, you ever see the movie Glen, Gary, Glen Ross?
我是说，你看过《拜金一族》那部电影吗？

668
00:29:15.360 --> 00:29:15.900
Well, I'm Ross.
嗯，我就是那个罗斯。

669
00:29:16.760 --> 00:29:18.100
I've never seen that movie.
我从没看过那部电影。

670
00:29:18.200 --> 00:29:19.780
And that's not how we do business.
而且我们做生意可不是那样。

671
00:29:19.960 --> 00:29:21.080
I know the general giSt.
我大概知道是什么意思。

672
00:29:21.300 --> 00:29:22.400
We're on the up and up.
我们可是光明正大的。

673
00:29:22.900 --> 00:29:24.400
But it is exciting.
但这确实很刺激。

674
00:29:24.820 --> 00:29:32.120
I mean, I don't know what you guys have been doing following this lady around, but this is the real estate game.
我是说，我不知道你们为什么要跟着这位女士转，但这才是房地产行业的真谛。

675
00:29:32.700 --> 00:29:33.460
Look at that.
看看那个。

676
00:29:33.640 --> 00:29:34.480
Look at that.
看看那个。

677
00:29:35.260 --> 00:29:36.160
You feel that energy?
感受到那种能量了吗？

678
00:29:38.600 --> 00:29:40.060
They're coiled springs.
他们就像蓄势待发的弹簧。

679
00:29:42.700 --> 00:29:44.400
Following this lady around.
跟着这位女士转。

680
00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:51.380
Also, when he goes, look at that, it's just everyone ignoring him, just doing, like, their mundane tasks.
还有，当他说“看看那个”的时候，每个人都在无视他，只是在做些琐碎的工作。

681
00:29:51.380 --> 00:29:55.200
And then here's the talking head by the Jim-esque character.
接下来是那个类似吉姆的角色的采访镜头。

682
00:29:55.640 --> 00:30:02.100
My best friends in this office are Cut the Rope, Angry Birds, Minesweeper.
我在办公室里最好的朋友是《割绳子》、《愤怒的小鸟》和《扫雷》。

683
00:30:02.620 --> 00:30:04.340
Still playing Minesweeper.
还在玩《扫雷》呢。

684
00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:10.700
But as far as human contact around here, nah, I do my best to avoid it.
至于这儿的人际交往，算了吧，我尽量避开。

685
00:30:11.680 --> 00:30:13.240
I love both of those.
这两个我都超爱。

686
00:30:13.360 --> 00:30:14.040
I know, right?
对吧？

687
00:30:14.180 --> 00:30:14.920
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

688
00:30:15.300 --> 00:30:24.240
I get cutting them because if we give those characters talking heads, it's like we're starting to get, I think, a little too down the rabbit hole with that business.
我理解为什么要删掉，因为如果我们给那些角色安排采访镜头，我觉得就有点太深陷于那条支线剧情了。

689
00:30:24.520 --> 00:30:24.660
Yeah.
是啊。

690
00:30:24.660 --> 00:30:25.880
I just don't think it needed it.
我只是觉得没必要。

691
00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:26.100
No.
没错。

692
00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:26.400
Yeah.
是啊。

693
00:30:26.940 --> 00:30:29.980
Well, Pam is going to leave this real estate office forever now.
好了，帕姆现在要永远离开这家房地产办公室了。

694
00:30:30.180 --> 00:30:36.280
But before we leave this real estate office, Angela and I need to give a shout out to Kristen S.
但在离开这家房地产办公室之前，安吉拉和我得向来自费城的克里斯汀·S表示感谢。

695
00:30:36.440 --> 00:30:36.880
from Philly.
来自费城的。

696
00:30:37.140 --> 00:30:38.000
Yes, we do.
没错，必须得感谢。

697
00:30:38.260 --> 00:30:40.660
Talk about a heck of a background catch.
真是一个了不起的背景细节捕捉。

698
00:30:41.600 --> 00:30:44.540
In this office, there's a big whiteboard.
在这个办公室里，有一块很大的白板。

699
00:30:44.720 --> 00:30:44.940
Yep.
没错。

700
00:30:45.180 --> 00:30:46.600
And it has a bunch of writing on it.
上面写着一堆东西。

701
00:30:47.020 --> 00:30:48.720
Angela, I know you paused on it.
安吉拉，我知道你刚才停在那儿了。

702
00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:49.340
I did.
我确实停了。

703
00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:49.940
Of course.
当然。

704
00:30:50.260 --> 00:30:54.960
And then I saw what Kristen wrote in and I thought, oh, my gosh, she covered it all.
然后我看到了克里斯汀写的内容，我想，天哪，她全都涵盖了。

705
00:30:55.300 --> 00:30:56.220
She sure did.
她确实涵盖了。

706
00:30:56.660 --> 00:30:58.140
Here's what's on that whiteboard.
白板上写的是这些。

707
00:30:58.400 --> 00:31:01.640
It's a bunch of street names, basically, addresses.
基本上是一堆街道名称，也就是地址。

708
00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:03.260
You know, this is a real estate office.
你知道，这是一家房地产办公室。

709
00:31:03.720 --> 00:31:05.300
Here's what Kristen had to say.
这是克里斯汀的看法。

710
00:31:05.300 --> 00:31:15.480
While there are a handful of streets that don't track with real addresses, like Jonesburg Place and Rhinehurst Lane, many of the streets are real.
虽然有少数几条街道与真实地址不符，比如琼斯堡广场和莱茵赫斯特巷，但很多街道都是真实存在的。

711
00:31:15.760 --> 00:31:23.720
They are well-known center city streets like Delancey, Pine Street, South Street, Locust, Gerard Avenue, and even Penn Square,
它们是市中心众所周知的街道，比如德兰西街、松树街、南街、蝗虫街、杰拉德大道，甚至还有佩恩广场，

712
00:31:23.720 --> 00:31:27.680
as well as smaller streets like Woodbine and Gravers Lane.
以及像伍德拜恩街和格雷弗斯巷这样的小街道。

713
00:31:27.840 --> 00:31:32.740
But what's really brilliant is that in many cases, the unit numbers track with the property type.
但真正精彩的是，在许多情况下，单元号与房产类型是相符的。

714
00:31:32.740 --> 00:31:43.040
And then she says, for example, commercial real estate in Center City has unit numbers that match for a tall office building that would be in that location.
她还说，例如，市中心的商业地产的单元号与该地段的高层办公楼相匹配。

715
00:31:44.460 --> 00:31:52.220
1420 Market Street isn't a real address, but it would be in the heart of downtown and would likely have a 20th floor unit, as noted.
市场街1420号不是一个真实的地址，但它位于市中心，正如所指出的，很可能会有20楼的单元。

716
00:31:53.500 --> 00:32:01.520
While others in more apartment-dense neighborhoods track like apartment units, like 1842 Pine Street, No.
而公寓密集区的其他地址则像公寓单元一样，比如松树街1842号，10号房。

717
00:32:01.620 --> 00:32:02.060
10.
10号。

718
00:32:02.620 --> 00:32:09.300
And areas that are dense with single-family homes, like 8412 Gerard, track just as well.
而像杰拉德街8412号这样独栋住宅密集的区域，也同样如此。

719
00:32:09.740 --> 00:32:15.420
What I think is brilliant about this is that none of these are real addresses you could find by walking.
我觉得这最精彩的地方在于，这些都不是你在街上走着就能找到的真实地址。

720
00:32:15.420 --> 00:32:21.120
For example, so while there is a Penn Square, there isn't a 1224 South Penn Square.
例如，虽然有佩恩广场，但并没有南佩恩广场1224号。

721
00:32:21.320 --> 00:32:26.680
But kudos to the team for inventing realistic places that also aren't real.
但还是要为团队点赞，他们发明了既逼真又不存在的地方。

722
00:32:26.920 --> 00:32:28.200
That's pretty amazing.
这太令人惊叹了。

723
00:32:28.580 --> 00:32:31.980
I mean, I love that attention to detail.
我是说，我喜欢这种对细节的关注。

724
00:32:32.120 --> 00:32:33.980
They could have just scribbled anything up there.
他们本可以随便在上面乱涂乱画的。

725
00:32:34.120 --> 00:32:40.620
But the time that they took to make that track for real is just kudos to our set deck.
但他们花时间让这些看起来如此真实，真得为我们的布景师点赞。

726
00:32:40.620 --> 00:32:45.300
I'm always impressed by all the amounts of detail, even in Aunt Shirley's home.
我总是对所有的细节量感到印象深刻，即使是在雪莉阿姨的家里。

727
00:32:45.920 --> 00:32:49.520
I was going to break down everything in Aunt Shirley's home, but there's so much clutter.
我本来打算把雪莉阿姨家里的所有东西都分析一遍，但那里的杂物太多了。

728
00:32:50.940 --> 00:32:55.560
But Kristen, I loved your background catch of everything on the whiteboard.
不过克里斯汀，我很喜欢你对白板上所有内容的背景捕捉。

729
00:32:55.780 --> 00:32:56.620
That was fantastic.
那太棒了。

730
00:32:57.480 --> 00:32:58.500
And you know what?
你知道吗？

731
00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:03.920
If there was a whiteboard that was supposedly representing my hometown of St. Louis—
如果有一块白板本应代表我的家乡圣路易斯——

732
00:33:03.920 --> 00:33:04.760
I'd be curious.
我会很好奇。

733
00:33:04.760 --> 00:33:08.600
It would be, like, glaringly obvious to me if it was all fakie.
如果全是假的话，对我来说会非常明显。

734
00:33:08.600 --> 00:33:13.140
And so I love that someone from Philly was like, yes!
所以我很喜欢有个费城人说，没错！

735
00:33:13.840 --> 00:33:14.020
Yeah.
是的。

736
00:33:14.580 --> 00:33:18.700
Up next, Dwight is going to walk in on Angela braiding Aunt Shirley's hair.
接下来，德怀特会撞见安吉拉在给雪莉阿姨编辫子。

737
00:33:19.040 --> 00:33:23.660
Yes, I love her snarky remark that a woman of her age shouldn't have hair this long.
是的，我喜欢她那句刻薄的评论，说她这个年纪的女人不该留这么长的头发。

738
00:33:23.760 --> 00:33:25.120
That was an improv by me.
那是我即兴发挥的。

739
00:33:25.280 --> 00:33:25.700
What?
什么？

740
00:33:25.960 --> 00:33:26.360
Yes.
是的。

741
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:28.220
No, Angela, it's so funny.
不，安吉拉，那太搞笑了。

742
00:33:28.400 --> 00:33:29.180
It's true.
这是真的。

743
00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:30.520
It's an improv by me.
那是我即兴发挥的。

744
00:33:30.740 --> 00:33:33.140
The scene would have ended with Angela Martin saying,
原本那场戏应该以安吉拉·马丁说这句话结束：

745
00:33:33.320 --> 00:33:35.000
Loose braids reflect a loose character.
松散的辫子反映了松散的品行。

746
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:36.000
Now stay still.
现在别动。

747
00:33:36.480 --> 00:33:38.140
And Shirley would have said, yes, ma'am.
然后雪莉会说，好的，女士。

748
00:33:38.140 --> 00:33:39.680
That's the end of the scene.
那场戏就结束了。

749
00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:44.760
And then I improvised, I think your hair is much too long for your age, by the way.
然后我即兴加了一句，顺便说一下，我觉得你的头发对你的年龄来说太长了。

750
00:33:45.040 --> 00:33:46.360
And Shirley says, okay.
然后雪莉说，好的。

751
00:33:46.360 --> 00:33:47.440
And I say, there.
我说，在那儿。

752
00:33:47.580 --> 00:33:48.860
And she goes, thank you, Angela.
她说，谢谢你，安吉拉。

753
00:33:49.240 --> 00:33:51.080
I love that bit of improv.
我喜欢那段即兴发挥。

754
00:33:52.340 --> 00:33:53.420
That's so good.
太棒了。

755
00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:54.660
All right.
好吧。

756
00:33:54.660 --> 00:33:57.020
So now Toby is going to enter the kitchen.
现在托比要走进厨房了。

757
00:33:57.480 --> 00:33:59.740
Nellie and Daryl are sitting reading their newspapers.
奈莉和达里尔正坐着看报纸。

758
00:33:59.740 --> 00:34:05.120
And Toby's going to announce he's going to the prison to visit the Scranton Strangler.
托比要宣布他要去监狱探望斯克兰顿勒杀手。

759
00:34:05.480 --> 00:34:07.160
I had a fan catch.
我有个粉丝捕捉到了。

760
00:34:07.340 --> 00:34:07.700
Okay.
好的。

761
00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:11.900
That was also seen by Judy in Westerville, Ohio, and Catherine S.
俄亥俄州韦斯特维尔的朱迪和凯瑟琳·S也看到了这一点。

762
00:34:12.140 --> 00:34:13.340
in Nolensville, Tennessee.
在田纳西州的诺伦斯维尔。

763
00:34:14.120 --> 00:34:20.520
If you watch the shots of Nellie, her newspaper is, like, always in a different position.
如果你观察奈莉的镜头，她的报纸位置总是变来变去的。

764
00:34:20.740 --> 00:34:20.840
Oh, no.
哦，不。

765
00:34:20.840 --> 00:34:21.440
Every shot.
每个镜头都这样。

766
00:34:21.620 --> 00:34:26.860
They so clearly use different takes because, like, in one, she has it totally open.
很明显他们用了不同的拍摄片段，因为你看，在一个镜头里，报纸是完全摊开的。

767
00:34:27.040 --> 00:34:27.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

768
00:34:27.320 --> 00:34:29.080
And then another, it's folded in half.
然后在另一个镜头里，它又对折了。

769
00:34:29.320 --> 00:34:30.900
In one, she's reading the comics.
在一个镜头里，她在看漫画。

770
00:34:30.900 --> 00:34:32.880
And then in another, she's reading an article.
而在另一个镜头里，她在看文章。

771
00:34:33.440 --> 00:34:36.420
And I have to say, I feel like maybe she was really reading the newspaper.
我得说，我觉得她可能真的在看报纸。

772
00:34:36.740 --> 00:34:38.260
Because she was turning pages.
因为她在翻页。

773
00:34:38.420 --> 00:34:38.780
Yes.
是的。

774
00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:40.720
Like, between takes.
比如，在拍摄间隙。

775
00:34:41.140 --> 00:34:43.160
Pam has now left the real estate office.
帕姆现在离开了房地产办公室。

776
00:34:43.340 --> 00:34:45.160
She's back at Jim's apartment in Philly.
她回到了吉姆在费城的公寓。

777
00:34:45.220 --> 00:34:47.520
And he calls to ask her how the interview went.
他打电话问她面试情况如何。

778
00:34:47.620 --> 00:34:50.580
But before she can really get into it, he's like, you know what?
但她还没来得及细说，他就说，你知道吗？

779
00:34:50.680 --> 00:34:52.700
Tell me everything about it at 8 o'clock dinner.
晚上8点吃晚饭时再把一切都告诉我。

780
00:34:53.060 --> 00:34:54.320
He's going to have dinner for her.
他要为她准备晚餐。

781
00:34:54.420 --> 00:34:55.160
And she's like, okay.
