01:01:22.970 --> 01:01:30.410
shared last week about your online purchases, is that Oscar, he watches too many online ads
上周分享的关于你网购的事，奥斯卡看了太多的网络广告，

1416
01:01:30.410 --> 01:01:31.890
and he doesn't do enough sit-ups.
却没做足够的仰卧起坐。

1417
01:01:31.890 --> 01:01:37.410
So he bought ankle braces, which, by the way, he bought from an online ad, so he can
所以他买了护踝，顺便说一下，这也是他从网络广告上买的，这样他就能

1418
01:01:37.410 --> 01:01:40.990
get 30 seconds of ab blasting whenever an ad pops up.
在广告弹出时做30秒的腹肌训练。

1419
01:01:41.510 --> 01:01:42.510
Ads for abs.
广告练腹肌。

1420
01:01:42.510 --> 01:01:48.590
Well, this contraption is real, and Oscar did it.
这个装置是真的，奥斯卡也确实做了。

1421
01:01:48.750 --> 01:01:49.090
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1422
01:01:49.290 --> 01:01:54.990
He goes over and he hooks himself in upside down and starts doing some crunches.
他走过去，把自己倒挂在上面，开始做仰卧起坐。

1423
01:01:55.510 --> 01:02:00.450
Meanwhile, Angela and Phyllis are pushing him aside to get in and out of the kitchen.
与此同时，安吉拉和菲利斯把他挤到一边，进出厨房。

1424
01:02:00.710 --> 01:02:05.230
Yes, it was really fun to walk past him with just, like, my cup of coffee, like, excuse me.
是的，拿着咖啡杯从他身边走过真的很有趣，就像是，借过一下。

1425
01:02:06.150 --> 01:02:11.150
Well, we got a few fan questions, one from Ivy K in Harrisonburg, Virginia, who said,
我们收到了一些粉丝提问，一位来自弗吉尼亚州哈里森堡的艾薇·K问，

1426
01:02:11.290 --> 01:02:16.110
how long did Oscar have to hang from the sit-up contraption, and were there any safety meetings
奥斯卡在那个仰卧起坐装置上挂了多久，有没有进行过任何安全会议？

1427
01:02:16.110 --> 01:02:16.630
involved?
还有一位来自加拿大安大略省基奇纳的塞奇·L问，在奥斯卡的彩蛋里，

1428
01:02:17.190 --> 01:02:23.030
And another one from Sage L in Kitchener, Ontario, Canada, who said, in the button with
真的是他在做仰卧起坐吗？

1429
01:02:23.030 --> 01:02:25.310
Oscar, is that really him doing the sit-ups?
我们知道必须问问奥斯卡，他发来了一段音频。

1430
01:02:25.710 --> 01:02:29.810
Well, we knew we would have to ask Oscar about this, and he sent in an audio clip.
听听他是怎么说的。

1431
01:02:30.010 --> 01:02:31.110
Here's what he had to say.
嗨，安吉拉。

1432
01:02:31.810 --> 01:02:32.670
Hi, Angela.
嗨，珍娜。

1433
01:02:32.810 --> 01:02:33.190
Hi, Jenna.
让我想想。

1434
01:02:33.550 --> 01:02:33.930
Let's see.
真的是我在上面挂着吗？我们有开安全会议吗？真的是我在做仰卧起坐吗？

1435
01:02:34.090 --> 01:02:38.730
Was that me really hanging, and did we have safety meetings, and was that me doing sit-ups?
答案都是肯定的。

1436
01:02:39.890 --> 01:02:41.270
Yes to all of that.
我不记得了。

1437
01:02:41.450 --> 01:02:42.890
I don't remember.
我记得拍过这场戏。

1438
01:02:43.010 --> 01:02:44.370
I remember doing the scene.
我不记得前后具体发生了什么，因为那只是普通的一天。

1439
01:02:45.270 --> 01:02:50.330
I don't remember exactly what happened before and after, because it was just a regular day.
那是片场的一天，是很平常的一天。

1440
01:02:50.450 --> 01:02:53.310
It was a day on the set, which is a kind of a normal day.
那是很久以前的事了。

1441
01:02:53.310 --> 01:02:54.390
It was a long time ago.
所以我肯定我们开过安全会议，他们问我，奥斯卡，你觉得你能做

1442
01:02:54.930 --> 01:02:58.990
And so I'm sure we had a safety meeting, and they said, Oscar, do you think you can do
这个吗？

1443
01:02:58.990 --> 01:02:59.270
this?
我记得当时想，哦，这就像《美国舞男》里理查·基尔

1444
01:02:59.910 --> 01:03:04.910
I remember thinking, oh, this is like that scene in American Gigolo when Richard Gere
倒挂的那场戏。

1445
01:03:05.510 --> 01:03:06.630
hangs upside down.
我想那是一部80年代的电影。

1446
01:03:06.830 --> 01:03:08.390
This is a movie from the 80s, I think.
里面有金发女郎乐队唱的那首《Call Me》。

1447
01:03:08.990 --> 01:03:11.510
Had that song, Call Me, with Blondie.
总之，我肯定他们问我，嘿，你能做这个吗？

1448
01:03:12.110 --> 01:03:14.770
But anyway, so I'm sure they said, hey, can you do this?
我说，可以。

1449
01:03:14.830 --> 01:03:16.230
And I said, yes.
我不觉得当时有替身演员在场。

1450
01:03:16.470 --> 01:03:18.530
I don't think there was a stunt person there.
我不觉得当时有替身演员在场。

1451
01:03:18.610 --> 01:03:20.090
They probably offered one to me.
他们大概也给我提供了一个。

1452
01:03:20.850 --> 01:03:25.050
So I hung, and at the beginning, it was easy to do the sit-ups.
所以我挂在那儿，一开始做仰卧起坐还挺容易的。

1453
01:03:25.210 --> 01:03:26.950
As it went on, the scene, more takes.
随着拍摄进行，场景多了，拍摄次数也多了。

1454
01:03:27.130 --> 01:03:28.270
You get more and more tired.
你会越来越累。

1455
01:03:29.390 --> 01:03:30.790
But I think it was okay.
但我觉得还行。

1456
01:03:30.910 --> 01:03:33.690
Maybe towards the end, I needed help getting up towards the bar.
可能快结束的时候，我需要别人帮我一把才能起身够到横杆。

1457
01:03:34.290 --> 01:03:37.050
I think that might have happened towards the end.
我想快结束时可能确实发生了这种情况。

1458
01:03:37.830 --> 01:03:39.850
But I remember there were a lot of funny takes.
但我记得有很多搞笑的拍摄片段。

1459
01:03:40.570 --> 01:03:44.230
My wife, personally, reminded me of the one where, because she looked at it, where Angela
我妻子特意提醒我，有一个片段是因为她看了那个片段，安吉拉

1460
01:03:44.230 --> 01:03:46.990
walks by and pushes me aside like I'm a curtain hanging there.
走过来把我推到一边，就像我是挂在那儿的窗帘一样。

1461
01:03:48.670 --> 01:03:50.070
But that was me.
但那确实是我本人。

1462
01:03:50.390 --> 01:03:53.530
There were no stunt people used for that.
那场戏没用替身。

1463
01:03:53.770 --> 01:03:55.030
It wasn't that dangerous.
没那么危险。

1464
01:03:55.210 --> 01:03:59.470
It was just a weird scene that we did at the office.
那只是我们在办公室拍的一场奇怪的戏。

1465
01:04:00.410 --> 01:04:02.990
I remember his face getting red.
我记得他的脸都涨红了。

1466
01:04:03.690 --> 01:04:08.970
Well, it's funny you say that, because Steve Burgess sent me the test videos.
说来有趣，史蒂夫·伯吉斯把测试视频发给了我。

1467
01:04:09.390 --> 01:04:13.430
And it was Tim from Construction and John from Special Effects.
那是建筑组的蒂姆和特效组的约翰。

1468
01:04:13.670 --> 01:04:16.450
They put in the bar, and they tested it.
他们装上了横杆，并进行了测试。

1469
01:04:16.450 --> 01:04:20.490
And Tim hooked himself in, and he's hanging upside down.
蒂姆把自己挂了上去，头朝下倒挂着。

1470
01:04:20.490 --> 01:04:24.170
And they're like, hey, man, is the blood rushing to your head?
他们问他，嘿，伙计，血液是不是都冲到脑门了？

1471
01:04:24.190 --> 01:04:25.330
And he's like, it is.
他说，确实是。

1472
01:04:26.070 --> 01:04:29.470
And he was like, it's pretty easy to get in and out of.
他还说，进出这个装置还挺容易的。

1473
01:04:29.570 --> 01:04:31.430
But it was really hard to do the crunches.
但做卷腹真的很难。

1474
01:04:31.810 --> 01:04:36.610
But, Ang, they even practiced the bit where they kind of like push him aside to be like
不过，安吉，他们甚至还练习了把你或者菲利斯

1475
01:04:36.610 --> 01:04:37.570
you or Phyllis.
推开的那段戏。

1476
01:04:37.830 --> 01:04:40.090
So, yeah, they did an extensive teSt.
所以，没错，他们做了详尽的测试。

1477
01:04:40.490 --> 01:04:43.730
I did notice that Phyllis was like, I have hot coffee here.
我确实注意到菲利斯当时说，我这儿有热咖啡。

1478
01:04:43.730 --> 01:04:48.150
But she was holding her hand around the mug, not using the handles.
但她是用手握着杯身，而不是拿着把手。

1479
01:04:48.590 --> 01:04:48.730
Yes.
是的。

1480
01:04:48.870 --> 01:04:52.770
And then when she hands it to Stanley, he reacts as if it's super hot.
然后当她把咖啡递给斯坦利时，他的反应就像咖啡烫得不行一样。

1481
01:04:52.910 --> 01:04:53.510
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

1482
01:04:54.890 --> 01:05:00.890
Well, after all this business of hanging upside down, the camera goes back to Oscar's computer,
话说回来，在这一通倒挂的折腾之后，镜头切回了奥斯卡的电脑，

1483
01:05:00.890 --> 01:05:03.110
and we see an ad pop up.
我们看到弹出了一个广告。

1484
01:05:03.110 --> 01:05:09.170
And it says, coming this May, the office, an American workplace, 10 years in the making,
上面写着，今年五月即将播出，《办公室》，一部美式职场剧，历时十年打造，

1485
01:05:09.430 --> 01:05:13.950
a look at the lives and loves of an average American small business office.
带你一窥普通美国小企业办公室里的生活与爱。

1486
01:05:14.930 --> 01:05:17.390
And that's what the episode ends with.
这一集就在这里结束了。

1487
01:05:18.090 --> 01:05:19.130
My gosh.
天哪。

1488
01:05:19.590 --> 01:05:22.810
Well, I remember after that aired, all of our phones blowing up.
我记得那集播出后，我们的手机都被打爆了。

1489
01:05:22.950 --> 01:05:24.550
People were like, oh, my gosh.
人们都在说，天哪。

1490
01:05:24.950 --> 01:05:25.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1491
01:05:25.790 --> 01:05:30.290
Well, listen, before we go today, I wanted to read a letter that we got from Amy A.
好了，听着，在今天结束之前，我想读一封我们收到的信，来自艾米·A。

1492
01:05:30.470 --> 01:05:30.550
in
她住在

1493
01:05:30.550 --> 01:05:31.930
Bakersfield, California.
加利福尼亚州贝克斯菲尔德。

1494
01:05:32.150 --> 01:05:35.650
It's very emotional, but I was very moved by it.
这封信非常感人，我被深深触动了。

1495
01:05:35.870 --> 01:05:38.150
And I wanted to read it.
所以我想读一读。

1496
01:05:38.410 --> 01:05:38.550
Yeah.
好的。

1497
01:05:38.790 --> 01:05:39.530
So here we go.
那么我们开始吧。

1498
01:05:40.190 --> 01:05:44.030
Angela and Jenna, I don't have a question, but just some words of gratitude.
安吉拉和珍娜，我没有什么问题，只是想表达一些感激之情。

1499
01:05:44.590 --> 01:05:50.950
On November 22, 2023, I lost my husband, Zach, suddenly at the age of 38.
2023年11月22日，我失去了我的丈夫扎克，他年仅38岁，走得很突然。

1500
01:05:50.950 --> 01:05:56.030
For the next few months, I sulked and cried and couldn't really get out of bed.
接下来的几个月里，我郁郁寡欢，以泪洗面，几乎无法下床。

1501
01:05:56.530 --> 01:06:01.590
We spent 15 years together, and I didn't know what adult life was like without him guiding
我们在一起度过了15年，如果没有他的指引，我根本不知道成年人的生活是什么样。

1502
01:06:01.590 --> 01:06:02.150
our ship.
他就像我们这艘船的舵手。

1503
01:06:02.630 --> 01:06:08.470
On Valentine's Day this year, I decided to watch our office anniversary episode, Moving
今年情人节，我决定重温我们办公室纪念日的那一集，《继续前行》。

1504
01:06:08.470 --> 01:06:08.830
On.
（Moving On）

1505
01:06:09.570 --> 01:06:14.210
This was the first episode of The Office we ever watched together, and we found it by
那是我们一起看的第一集《办公室》，当时纯属偶然，因为2013年2月14日那一集首播时我们都病了，

1506
01:06:14.210 --> 01:06:21.010
accident because we were both sick February 14, 2013, when the episode first aired, and
我们只想躺在床上喝点热汤。

1507
01:06:21.010 --> 01:06:23.190
all we wanted to do was have soup in bed.
抱歉。

1508
01:06:24.210 --> 01:06:24.810
Sorry.
看完那一集后，我们就彻底入坑了。

1509
01:06:26.270 --> 01:06:28.630
After that episode, we were hooked.
我们一起成了《办公室》的粉丝，午休时经常互相提问，

1510
01:06:28.870 --> 01:06:33.830
We were office fans together and often quizzed each other during our lunch breaks and quoted
还总是引用剧里的台词。

1511
01:06:33.830 --> 01:06:35.290
lines to each other constantly.
因为他的离世，我落下了你们的播客节目，直到上周一重返工作岗位后才开始重新收听。

1512
01:06:35.910 --> 01:06:40.970
Because of his passing, I fell behind on your podcast episodes and began listening again
开车回家的路上我哭得泣不成声，因为你们的声音、你们的故事，还有关于这部剧的记忆，

1513
01:06:40.970 --> 01:06:43.050
last Monday after returning to work.
瞬间把我带回了和他在一起的时光。

1514
01:06:43.050 --> 01:06:48.030
I bawled on my drive home because your voices, your stories, and just memories of the show
日子依然很难熬，但当家里播放着你们的播客时，那种我丈夫依然陪伴在身边的感觉，给了我极大的平静。

1515
01:06:48.030 --> 01:06:50.050
took me right back to my time with him.
重温《办公室》并回想起我们之间所有的那些梗，让我露出了笑容。

1516
01:06:50.970 --> 01:06:56.070
The days are still very hard, but having your podcast on in my home, where my husband's
我会永远带着我们对《办公室》共同的热爱生活下去，以后每看一集，我大概都会又笑又哭。

1517
01:06:56.070 --> 01:06:59.610
presence is still very strong, gives me so much peace.
谢谢你们俩让我的生活重新找回了一些欢笑。

1518
01:07:00.770 --> 01:07:05.370
Watching The Office and remembering all of our inside jokes together makes me smile.
扎克也会很感激的。

1519
01:07:05.710 --> 01:07:10.830
I will carry our mutual love of The Office with me forever, and I will laugh and probably
怀着无比感激的心情，艾米。

1520
01:07:10.830 --> 01:07:13.450
also cry every time I watch an episode.
艾米，非常感谢你写信给我们。

1521
01:07:14.070 --> 01:07:17.750
Thank you both for bringing some laughter back into my life.
你知道，真的很难用言语来表达《办公室》这部剧能帮助人们度过这样的时刻，或者帮助人们建立联系、治愈伤痛，这对我们来说意味着什么。

1522
01:07:17.950 --> 01:07:19.570
Zach would be grateful too.
更不用说，珍和我现在能通过这个播客参与其中，

1523
01:07:19.790 --> 01:07:21.710
With so much gratitude, Amy.
陪伴在你的身边。

1524
01:07:28.460 --> 01:07:31.120
Amy, thank you so much for writing in.
我们只想把我们的爱送给你，我们一直把你放在心上。

1525
01:07:31.120 --> 01:07:38.760
And, you know, it's really just hard to put into words how much it means to us that The Office
是的。

1526
01:07:38.760 --> 01:07:43.980
as a show helps people through times like this or helps people connect or heal.
谢谢你让我们能陪伴着你。

1527
01:07:45.020 --> 01:07:51.040
And then on top of it, that in any way that Jen and I are a part of that now with the podcast
是的。

1528
01:07:51.040 --> 01:07:52.100
to be there for you.
我们爱你。

1529
01:07:53.080 --> 01:07:56.560
We just want to give you our love and we just hold you in our hearts.
我们爱你。

1530
01:07:57.300 --> 01:07:57.780
Yeah.
我们爱你们。

1531
01:07:58.480 --> 01:08:00.220
Thanks for letting us be there with you.
我们热爱做这件事。

1532
01:08:00.460 --> 01:08:00.780
Yeah.
而且我确实想让大家知道，克里德在我们刚才节目里和他聊过之后，又给我们发了一条短信，我想读一下他刚发来的内容。

1533
01:08:01.260 --> 01:08:01.860
We love you.
那是一首优美的诗。

1534
01:08:02.380 --> 01:08:03.280
We love you.
确实如此。

1535
01:08:03.280 --> 01:08:04.400
We love you guys.
克里德写道：

1536
01:08:04.620 --> 01:08:05.620
We love doing this.
既然今天早上如此机缘巧合，我想给你们分享我最喜欢的一句关于猫的名言，

1537
01:08:05.880 --> 01:08:15.420
And I do want you all to know that Creed texted us one last time since we spoke to him earlier
来自艾伦·瓦茨。

1538
01:08:15.420 --> 01:08:19.320
in the episode, and I wanted to read you the text he just sent us.
当猫从树上掉下来时，它会让自己彻底放松。

1539
01:08:19.460 --> 01:08:21.220
It's a beautiful poem.
猫会变得完全松弛，从而轻盈地落在地上。

1540
01:08:21.440 --> 01:08:22.220
It is.
但如果猫在快要掉下树时，突然下定决心不想掉下去，

1541
01:08:22.720 --> 01:08:23.520
Creed wrote,
它就会变得紧张僵硬，落地时就会变成一袋碎骨头。

1542
01:08:23.520 --> 01:08:29.460
Since this morning has been so serendipitous, I thought I'd send you my favorite cat quote
同样地，道家哲学认为，我们每个人在生命的每一刻，其实都在从树上掉下来。

1543
01:08:29.460 --> 01:08:31.280
from Alan Watts.
我们在一起度过了15年，如果没有他的指引，我根本不知道成年人的生活是什么样。

1544
01:08:32.300 --> 01:08:35.780
When a cat falls out of a tree, it lets go of itself.
他就像我们这艘船的舵手。

1545
01:08:36.080 --> 01:08:39.880
The cat becomes completely relaxed and lands lightly on the ground.
今年情人节，我决定重温我们办公室纪念日的那一集，《继续前行》。

1546
01:08:40.320 --> 01:08:45.320
But if a cat were about to fall out of a tree and suddenly make up its mind that it didn't
（Moving On）

1547
01:08:45.320 --> 01:08:51.340
want to fall, it would become tense and rigid and would be just a bag of broken bones upon
那是我们一起看的第一集《办公室》，当时纯属偶然，因为2013年2月14日那一集首播时我们都病了，

1548
01:08:51.340 --> 01:08:51.760
landing.
我们只想躺在床上喝点热汤。

1549
01:08:52.060 --> 01:08:57.060
In the same way, it is the philosophy of the Tao that we are all falling off a tree at
抱歉。

1550
01:08:57.060 --> 01:08:58.580
every moment of our lives.
看完那一集后，我们就彻底入坑了。

1551
01:08:58.720 --> 01:09:04.460
As a matter of fact, the moment we were born, we were kicked off a precipice and we are falling,
事实上，我们从出生那一刻起，就像被踢下了悬崖，一直在坠落，

1552
01:09:04.620 --> 01:09:06.640
and there is nothing that can stop it.
而且没有任何东西能阻止这一切。

1553
01:09:06.860 --> 01:09:11.900
So instead of living in a state of chronic tension and clinging to all sorts of things
所以，与其长期处于紧张状态，紧抓着各种事物不放，

1554
01:09:11.900 --> 01:09:17.460
that are actually falling with us because the whole world is impermanent, be like a cat.
而那些事物其实也在随我们一起坠落，因为整个世界都是无常的，不如像猫一样活着。

1555
01:09:17.460 --> 01:09:18.940
I love it.
我太喜欢这个比喻了。

1556
01:09:19.560 --> 01:09:26.640
Well, a big thank you to Rainn Wilson, Oscar Nunez, Dave Rogers, Steve Burgess, and Creed
非常感谢雷恩·威尔森、奥斯卡·努内兹、戴夫·罗杰斯、史蒂夫·伯吉斯和克里德·布拉顿

1557
01:09:26.640 --> 01:09:30.780
Bratton for brightening up this episode and to all of you.
让这一集变得如此精彩，也感谢你们所有人。

1558
01:09:30.920 --> 01:09:34.340
For writing in, sending your questions, your comments, and letters.
感谢你们写信、发来问题、评论和信件。

1559
01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:35.860
We love you so much.
我们非常爱你们。

1560
01:09:35.980 --> 01:09:39.560
And now we are going to play a little bit of Creed's new single,
现在我们要播放一小段克里德的新单曲，

1561
01:09:39.780 --> 01:09:42.200
Out Now, Turn the Corner of the Universe.
现已发布，歌名是《转过宇宙的角落》。

1562
01:09:42.200 --> 01:09:46.040
And we'll see you next week with our interview with Bob Odenkirk.
下周我们将带来对鲍勃·奥登科克的采访，下周见。

1563
01:09:52.160 --> 01:09:57.640
Another day just like the others, or so it seemed to me.
又是平凡的一天，至少对我来说是这样。

1564
01:09:59.860 --> 01:10:02.200
I daydream about tomorrow.
我幻想着明天。

1565
01:10:03.800 --> 01:10:05.880
How it might turn out to be.
幻想着它会变成什么样。

1566
01:10:07.960 --> 01:10:09.600
Our doubt is in remission.
我们的疑虑正在消退。

1567
01:10:11.820 --> 01:10:13.620
We don't buy into the hype.
我们不再盲目跟风。

1568
01:10:16.060 --> 01:10:18.080
No stealing from each other.
我们互不掠夺。

1569
01:10:20.230 --> 01:10:21.730
We keep our family tight.
我们紧紧守护着家人。

1570
01:10:45.380 --> 01:10:47.140
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1571
01:10:47.140 --> 01:10:51.580
